{"id":"000W0J","title":"2's a Crowd (sandwich, skyscraper, numbered rooms)","author":"Chilly","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-12T12:51:14+00:00","posted":"Heute, 11:40 Uhr","rules":"I am continuing with my schedule of publishing back catalogue puzzles interspersed with newer trickier puzzles. Here is another one I worked on a few years ago when I was experimenting with dual outside clues. Please enjoy.\n\nThe Rules:\n\n• Normal Sudoku rules apply.\n• Numbered rooms: clues outside the grid in a pink circle are numbered rooms clues, and indicate the digit which has to be placed in the Nth cell in the corresponding direction, where N is the digit placed in the first cell in that direction.\n• Skyscraper: clues outside the grid in a green circle are skyscraper clues, and indicate how many digits are 'seen' looking into the grid along the respective row or column. Digits are visible only when larger than all the other digits that appear before them in line of sight.\n• Dual clues: clues outside the grid in two blue circles are both sandwich and skyscraper clues. Sandwich clues indicate the sum of the digits sandwiched between the 1 and 9 in the respective row or column.\n• Cages: digits in cages must sum to the value in the top left corner of the cage.\n\n2's a Crowd\nby Chilly\n\nLink for solving on Sudokupad","solutionCode":"Row 6","tags":["Sudoku","Sandwich (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/mc9hhmnk0y","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/mc9hhmnk0y","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":6,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-12T12:51:14+00:00"}